      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T09:44:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A device that reports a model by revision gets it reported missing when the only copy is stored under its openconfig-version and its latest revision has no semver reference, although that copy is exactly the requested revision. readRevision() at line 599 already accepts such a copy through latestRevisionOf. Could this fallback do the same before giving up? Also please add a test next to unreferencedRevisionTest() that requests the LATEST revision, not one from the history.",
      "revId": "e00c50386c95e261b78550db8c52f32e38c2812b",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12f111c6_b155dd35",
        "filename": "modules/gnmi-sb/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/gnmi/southbound/schema/impl/SchemaContextHolderImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 240,
      "author": {
        "id": 9229
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T12:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. The fallback now accepts a copy whose latest revision is the requested one, before comparing copies stored under revisions, the same way readRevision() does.",
      "parentUuid": "5b4b9baa_f347f536",
      "revId": "e00c50386c95e261b78550db8c52f32e38c2812b",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ddb1475_8146a722",
        "filename": "modules/gnmi-sb/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/gnmi/southbound/schema/impl/SchemaContextHolderImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 568,
