        "id": 8324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T09:44:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The revision-date first ordering only applies within one level of the dependency walk. If a module is pinned one level above a revision-date import of the same module, the pin wins and the parser fails with \"Imported module not found\", although a stored copy satisfies both. The fact that this issue exists means that no test covers it. And that\u0027s weird - we need to have it covered.",
      "revId": "e00c50386c95e261b78550db8c52f32e38c2812b",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f6188a7_a74311c5",
        "filename": "modules/gnmi-sb/src/main/java/org/opendaylight/gnmi/southbound/schema/impl/SchemaContextHolderImpl.java",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 568,
      "author": {
        "id": 9229
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-26T12:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When a revision-date import is found deeper in the walk than another requirement of the same model and the copy already read is not that revision, the revision is remembered and the models are read again with it required, so the result is the same as if both requirements met on one level.",
      "parentUuid": "6ddb1475_8146a722",
      "revId": "e00c50386c95e261b78550db8c52f32e38c2812b",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
